IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-period.l4: Chapter 10, ss 442 and 443 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): the period allowed for filing
-- accounts and reports, and how a period of months is calculated. Lines 5908-5935 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). A decision function that can say
-- "not covered" answers MAYBE: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`), NOTHING where it does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). The two functions that compute a date from dates answer a DATE:
-- the text gives a date for every input, so there is no "no" and no "not covered" in them.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- DAYS. All periods here are CALENDAR MONTHS counted by s 443, not by the daydate library's `add months`: s 443(3) ends a
-- period on the LAST day of the appropriate month when the specified date is the last day of its month, which `add months`
-- (it clamps) does not do (30 April 2025 plus 9 months: s 443 says 31 January 2026, `add months` says 30 January 2026).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 443: calculation of period allowed
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5928 | (1) This section applies for the purposes of calculating the period for filing a company's accounts and reports which is expressed as a specified number of months from a specified date or after the end of a specified previous period.
@ref s 443(1) Calculation of period allowed: when the section applies (src:5928)
GIVEN `the period for filing is expressed as a specified number of months from a specified date or after the end of a specified previous period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443(1) section 443 applies to the period for filing` MEANS
    IF `the period for filing is expressed as a specified number of months from a specified date or after the end of a specified previous period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which is expressed as a specified number of months from a specified date or after the end of a specified previous period"

-- src:5935 | (5) “The appropriate month” means the month that is the specified number of months after the month in which the specified date, or the end of the specified previous period, falls.
@ref s 443(5) The appropriate month (src:5935)
GIVEN `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` IS A DATE
      `the specified number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 443(5) the appropriate month` MEANS
    ((((DATE_MONTH `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`) MINUS 1) PLUS `the specified number of months`) MODULO 12) PLUS 1

-- The year in which the appropriate month falls (s 443(5) speaks of "the month", and a month belongs to a year).
-- src:5935 | (5) “The appropriate month” means the month that is the specified number of months after the month in which the specified date, or the end of the specified previous period, falls.
@ref s 443(5) The appropriate month: its year (src:5935)
GIVEN `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` IS A DATE
      `the specified number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 443(5) the year of the appropriate month` MEANS
    (DATE_YEAR `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`)
    PLUS (FLOOR ((((DATE_MONTH `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`) MINUS 1) PLUS `the specified number of months`) DIVIDED BY 12))

-- src:5930 | (3) If the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period, is the last day of a month, the period ends with the last day of the appropriate month (whether or not that is the corresponding date).
@ref s 443(3) The last day of a month (src:5930)
GIVEN `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 443(3) the specified date is the last day of a month` MEANS
    (DATE_DAY `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`)
    EQUALS `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`) (DATE_YEAR `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`)

-- src:5931 | (4) If—
-- src:5932 | (a) the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period, is not the last day of a month but is the 29th or 30th, and
-- src:5933 | (b) the appropriate month is February,
-- src:5934 | the period ends with the last day of February.
@ref s 443(4) The 29th or 30th and the appropriate month is February (src:5931-5934)
GIVEN `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` IS A DATE
      `the specified number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 443(4) the specified date is the 29th or 30th but not the last day of a month and the appropriate month is February` MEANS
        (NOT (`s 443(3) the specified date is the last day of a month` `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`))
    AND (   (DATE_DAY `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`) EQUALS 29
         OR (DATE_DAY `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`) EQUALS 30)
    AND (`s 443(5) the appropriate month` `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` `the specified number of months`) EQUALS 2

-- s 443(2) to (4) together: the date the period ends with. The text gives a date for every input.
-- src:5929 | (2) Subject to the following provisions, the period ends with the date in the appropriate month corresponding to the specified date or the last day of the specified previous period.
-- src:5930 | (3) If the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period, is the last day of a month, the period ends with the last day of the appropriate month (whether or not that is the corresponding date).
-- src:5931 | (4) If—
-- src:5932 | (a) the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period, is not the last day of a month but is the 29th or 30th, and
-- src:5933 | (b) the appropriate month is February,
-- src:5934 | the period ends with the last day of February.
@ref s 443(2) The period ends with the date in the appropriate month (src:5929-5934)
GIVEN `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` IS A DATE
      `the specified number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 443(2) the period ends with` MEANS
    LET month MEANS `s 443(5) the appropriate month` `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` `the specified number of months`
        year MEANS `s 443(5) the year of the appropriate month` `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` `the specified number of months`
    IN IF `s 443(3) the specified date is the last day of a month` `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`
       THEN Date (`Days in month` month year) month year
       ELSE IF `s 443(4) the specified date is the 29th or 30th but not the last day of a month and the appropriate month is February` `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period` `the specified number of months`
            THEN Date (`Days in month` 2 year) 2 year
            ELSE Date (DATE_DAY `the specified date, or the last day of the specified previous period`) month year

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 442: period allowed for filing accounts
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5925 | (6) Whether the period allowed is that for a private company or a public company is determined by reference to the company's status immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period.
@ref s 442(6) Status immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period (src:5925)
GIVEN `the company's status immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period (TRUE for a public company)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's status at any other time (TRUE for a public company)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 442(6) the period for a public company applies` MEANS
    -- The text decides by "the company's status immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period"; any other time is ignored.
    `the company's status immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period (TRUE for a public company)`

-- src:5926 | (7) In this section “the relevant accounting reference period” means the accounting reference period by reference to which the financial year for the accounts in question was determined.
@ref s 442(7) The relevant accounting reference period (src:5926)
GIVEN `the financial year for the accounts in question was determined by reference to the accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 442(7) the accounting reference period is the relevant accounting reference period` MEANS
    IF `the financial year for the accounts in question was determined by reference to the accounting reference period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant accounting reference period” means the accounting reference period by reference to which the financial year for the accounts in question was determined"

-- src:5911 | (2) The period is—
-- src:5912 | (a) for a private company, nine months after the end of the relevant accounting reference period, and
-- src:5913 | (b) for a public company, six months after the end of that period.
-- src:5914 | This is subject to the following provisions of this section.
@ref s 442(2) The period: nine months for a private company, six months for a public company (src:5911-5914)
GIVEN `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 442(2) the period for filing ends on` MEANS
    IF `the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period`
    THEN `s 443(2) the period ends with` `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` 6
    ELSE `s 443(2) the period ends with` `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` 9

-- "a period of more than twelve months": the period is longer than twelve months when it ends on or after the day twelve
-- calendar months after it began (a period from 15 January 2025 to 14 January 2026 is twelve months and no more).
-- src:5915 | (3) If the relevant accounting reference period is the company's first and is a period of more than twelve months, the period is—
@ref s 442(3) The relevant accounting reference period is the company's first and is a period of more than twelve months (src:5915)
GIVEN `the first day of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 442(3) the relevant accounting reference period is a period of more than twelve months` MEANS
    `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` AT LEAST (`add months` `the first day of the relevant accounting reference period` 12)

-- src:5915 | (3) If the relevant accounting reference period is the company's first and is a period of more than twelve months, the period is—
-- src:5916 | (a) nine months or six months, as the case may be, from the first anniversary of the incorporation of the company, or
-- src:5917 | (b) three months after the end of the accounting reference period,
-- src:5918 | whichever last expires.
@ref s 442(3) First accounting reference period of more than twelve months: whichever last expires (src:5915-5918)
GIVEN `the date of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 442(3) the period for filing ends on for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months` MEANS
    LET months MEANS IF `the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period` THEN 6 ELSE 9
        `the first anniversary of the incorporation` MEANS `add years` `the date of the company's incorporation` 1
        `nine months or six months, as the case may be, from the first anniversary` MEANS `s 443(2) the period ends with` `the first anniversary of the incorporation` months
        `three months after the end of the accounting reference period` MEANS `s 443(2) the period ends with` `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` 3
    IN IF `nine months or six months, as the case may be, from the first anniversary` AT LEAST `three months after the end of the accounting reference period`
       THEN `nine months or six months, as the case may be, from the first anniversary`
       ELSE `three months after the end of the accounting reference period`

-- src:5919 | (4) If the relevant accounting reference period is treated as shortened by virtue of a notice given by the company under section 392 (alteration of accounting reference date), the period is—
-- src:5920 | (a) that applicable in accordance with the above provisions, or
-- src:5921 | (b) three months from the date of the notice under that section,
-- src:5922 | whichever last expires.
@ref s 442(4) Accounting reference period treated as shortened by a notice under section 392 (src:5919-5922)
GIVEN `the period for filing that subsections (2) and (3) give` IS A DATE
      `the relevant accounting reference period is treated as shortened by virtue of a notice given by the company under section 392` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notice under section 392` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 442(4) the period for filing ends on where the accounting reference period is treated as shortened` MEANS
    IF `the relevant accounting reference period is treated as shortened by virtue of a notice given by the company under section 392`
    THEN LET `three months from the date of the notice` MEANS `s 443(2) the period ends with` `the date of the notice under section 392` 3
         IN IF `the period for filing that subsections (2) and (3) give` AT LEAST `three months from the date of the notice`
            THEN `the period for filing that subsections (2) and (3) give`
            ELSE `three months from the date of the notice`
    ELSE `the period for filing that subsections (2) and (3) give`

-- s 442(5): a power of the Secretary of State, encoded for what it means to a company's directors: whether the period can
-- be extended, and by when an application must be made. "if for any special reason the Secretary of State thinks fit" is
-- a judgment the text hands to him: a plain input, never guessed.
-- src:5923 | (5) Subject to subsection (5A), if for any special reason the Secretary of State thinks fit he may, on an application made before the expiry of the period otherwise allowed, by notice in writing to a company extend that period by such further period as may be specified in the notice.
@ref s 442(5) Extension by the Secretary of State (src:5923)
GIVEN `the date on which the period for filing would otherwise end` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the application was made` IS A DATE
      `for a special reason the Secretary of State thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 442(5) the Secretary of State may extend the period for filing` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the application was made` AT MOST `the date on which the period for filing would otherwise end`
    THEN IF `for a special reason the Secretary of State thinks fit`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if for any special reason the Secretary of State thinks fit he may"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on an application made before the expiry of the period otherwise allowed"

-- src:5924 | (5A) Any such extension must not have the effect of extending the period for filing to more than twelve months after the end of the relevant accounting reference period.
@ref s 442(5A) An extension must not take the period for filing beyond twelve months after the end of the accounting reference period (src:5924)
GIVEN `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the date to which the notice extends the period for filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 442(5A) the extension complies with the limit of twelve months after the end of the accounting reference period` MEANS
    IF `the date to which the notice extends the period for filing` AT MOST (`s 443(2) the period ends with` `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` 12)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such extension must not have the effect of extending the period for filing to more than twelve months after the end of the relevant accounting reference period"

-- src:5923 | (5) Subject to subsection (5A), if for any special reason the Secretary of State thinks fit he may, on an application made before the expiry of the period otherwise allowed, by notice in writing to a company extend that period by such further period as may be specified in the notice.
-- src:5924 | (5A) Any such extension must not have the effect of extending the period for filing to more than twelve months after the end of the relevant accounting reference period.
@ref s 442(5), (5A) The period for filing after an extension (src:5923-5924)
GIVEN `the period for filing before any extension` IS A DATE
      `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the Secretary of State has given a notice extending the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date to which the notice extends the period for filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 442(5A) the period for filing ends on after any extension` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Secretary of State has given a notice extending the period for filing`
    THEN JUST `the period for filing before any extension`
    ELSE IF `s 442(5A) the extension complies with the limit of twelve months after the end of the accounting reference period` `the end of the relevant accounting reference period` `the date to which the notice extends the period for filing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST `the date to which the notice extends the period for filing`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text forbids an extension beyond the limit but does not say what the notice then achieves

-- The facts the whole of s 442 reads, in one record that a caller (the seat layer) builds from what a person can state.
DECLARE `s 442 facts about the accounting reference period` HAS
    `s 442 the first day of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
    `s 442 the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A DATE
    `s 442 the relevant accounting reference period is the company's first` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 442 the date of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE
    `s 442 the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 442 the period is treated as shortened by virtue of a notice under section 392` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 442 the date of the notice under section 392` IS A DATE
    `s 442 the Secretary of State has given a notice extending the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 442 the date to which the notice extends the period for filing` IS A DATE

-- src:5909 | (1) This section specifies the period allowed for the directors of a company to comply with their obligation under section 441 to deliver accounts and reports for a financial year to the registrar.
-- src:5910 | This is referred to in the Companies Acts as the “period for filing” those accounts and reports.
@ref s 442(1) The period allowed for filing, "the period for filing" (src:5909-5910)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 442 facts about the accounting reference period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 442(1) the period for filing ends on` MEANS
    LET `the period for filing that subsections (2) and (3) give` MEANS
            IF     facts's `s 442 the relevant accounting reference period is the company's first`
               AND `s 442(3) the relevant accounting reference period is a period of more than twelve months` (facts's `s 442 the first day of the relevant accounting reference period`) (facts's `s 442 the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)
            THEN `s 442(3) the period for filing ends on for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months`
                    (facts's `s 442 the date of the company's incorporation`)
                    (facts's `s 442 the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)
                    (facts's `s 442 the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)
            ELSE `s 442(2) the period for filing ends on`
                    (facts's `s 442 the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)
                    (facts's `s 442 the company was a public company immediately before the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)
        `the period after any shortening` MEANS
            `s 442(4) the period for filing ends on where the accounting reference period is treated as shortened`
                `the period for filing that subsections (2) and (3) give`
                (facts's `s 442 the period is treated as shortened by virtue of a notice under section 392`)
                (facts's `s 442 the date of the notice under section 392`)
    IN `s 442(5A) the period for filing ends on after any extension`
           `the period after any shortening`
           (facts's `s 442 the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)
           (facts's `s 442 the Secretary of State has given a notice extending the period for filing`)
           (facts's `s 442 the date to which the notice extends the period for filing`)

-- WITHIN for a regulative rule (s 441) counts days: the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period
-- to the end of the period for filing. NOTHING when s 442(1) is NOTHING.
-- src:5909 | (1) This section specifies the period allowed for the directors of a company to comply with their obligation under section 441 to deliver accounts and reports for a financial year to the registrar.
@ref s 442(1) The period for filing, in days from the end of the accounting reference period (src:5909)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 442 facts about the accounting reference period`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 442(1) the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 442(1) the period for filing ends on` facts
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN JUST ((Day `the last day`) MINUS (Day (facts's `s 442 the end of the relevant accounting reference period`)))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 442(5A) gives no period for filing when an extension passes the limit
